course: dictionary
lesson: 4410
title: Halloween: a festival with a long name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Halloween is the name of a festival, so it starts with a capital letter. It is held in the evening at the very end of October. «Halloween on 31 October grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival at the end of the harvest.»
explain: Context clues tell you what happens at Halloween. Words like costumes, pumpkins and spooky show that it is a night of dressing up and spooky fun. Trick-or-treat means going door to door for sweets, so it is a clue to a festival about treats.
explain: The name is a clue too. «Halloween's name comes from All Hallows' Eve, the night before All Saints' Day.» Hallows means holy people, and Eve means the evening before, so the name tells you when the festival is.
explain: Stay safe on Halloween. Go trick-or-treating with an adult or a group, carry a torch, wear bright or reflective costumes, check your sweets with an adult, and only visit houses you know.
fact: Halloween is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Halloween is held on 31 October, in the evening at the very end of the month.
fact: «Halloween's name comes from All Hallows' Eve, the night before All Saints' Day.»
fact: Its old meaning is All Hallows' Eve, the evening before All Saints' Day.
fact: Halloween grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival, and is celebrated in the USA, Canada, the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
exercise: «Halloween on 31 October grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival.» Which date is Halloween? | 5 November | 25 December | 1 January | *31 October
exercise: Why does Halloween start with a capital letter? | Because it is at the start of a sentence | Because it is a verb | Because it is always written in bold | *Because it is the name of a special day, a proper noun
exercise: What should you do when you go trick-or-treating? | Visit any house, even one you do not know | Eat every sweet before you get home | Go alone in the dark with no torch | *Go with an adult or a group and carry a torch
test: What do people carve on Halloween? | Eggs, into Easter baskets | *Pumpkins, into jack-o'-lanterns | Snowmen, into a line | Candles, into birthday cakes
test: What is the old meaning of Halloween? | *The evening before All Saints' Day | The day after Christmas | The end of the summer holidays | A type of costume
exam: Which spelling is correct for the name of the festival? | *Halloween | halloween | HALLOWEEN | halLoween
